Package: winstepsR
Title: Generate Winsteps Input Files, Run Winsteps, and Read Its Output
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Anthony", "Raborn", email = "anthony@raborndecisionsciences.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A thin, organization-agnostic interface between R and the Rasch
    measurement program Winsteps. Given item response data in long format
    and a set of anchored item difficulties, winstepsR writes the Winsteps
    person-response data file, item anchor file, and control file; runs
    Winsteps in batch mode; and reads the resulting person output file
    (PFILE) back into R as a tibble. It intentionally does not implement
    any exam-specific scoring rules (scale-score conversions, penalty
    rules, domain definitions, etc.) -- those belong in the calling
    project, not in this package.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    tidyr,
    readr,
    tibble,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
